    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0348" n="244" xml:id="pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4004 Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Switzerland
                        (Wilson), at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-06T20:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Your No. 9, February 6, 1 p.m. With regard to my views on question of the
                    course which may best be pursued in the light of the Japanese reply to the
                    suggestions advanced by the American and other governments, it is suggested that
                    you inquire of Sir John Simon.</p>
                <p>For your confidential information, he is aware of my views and you may inform him
                    that I have so informed you.</p>
                <p>The foregoing is confidential to you and to Sir John Simon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
